  "_skill_md": "---\nname: moltbook\ndescription: Internal API for moltbook\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://www.moltbook.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Cookie-based (__Host-authjs.csrf-token)\"\n  endpointCount: 7\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"web-app\"\n---\n\n# Moltbook API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nCookie-based (__Host-authjs.csrf-token) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Data Read (4)\n- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve a specific Moltbook entry by its ID.\n- `GET /developers/apply` — Get information about applying to be a developer.\n- `GET /m/general` — Retrieve general Moltbook information.\n- `GET /post/{postId}` — Fetch a specific post by its ID.\n\n### Media (1)\n- `GET /_next/image` — Download an image from Moltbook's CDN.\n\n### Core API (2)\n- `GET /api/v1/{id}/{id}` — Access a core Moltbook API endpoint (two IDs).\n- `GET /api/v1/{id}/{id}/{id}` — Access a core Moltbook API endpoint (three IDs).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"moltbook\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere's a \"Quick Start\" section for your reverse-engineered API skill document:\n\n```typescript\n// Retrieve a specific Moltbook entry by its ID.\nconst entry = await client.getEntry({ id: \"someEntryId\" });\nconsole.log(entry);\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Fetch a specific post by its ID.\nconst post = await client.getPost({ postId: \"12345\" });\nconsole.log(post);\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Cookie-based (__Host-authjs.csrf-token)\n**Base URL:** `https://www.moltbook.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 4 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Moltbook's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Moltbook data without official API access\n- Automate actions on www.moltbook.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Moltbook frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { MoltbookClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await MoltbookClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 0 (none)\n- **Session cookies:** 4\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (11)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
